meta {
  name: Bulk Update Tasks
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/tasks/bulk
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "ids": ["{{taskId}}"],
    "status_name": "in_progress",
    "note": "Picked up in bulk"
  }
}

docs {
  Requires tasks.bulk AND tasks.edit (403 without either). 1-100 ids; provide assignee_id (uuid or null to
  unassign) and/or status_name. Reassigning to anyone other than yourself also needs
  tasks.assign. Each id is authorised like a single PATCH and runs in its own transaction:
  the response is { results: [{ id, ok, error? }], updated, failed } and a task you may
  not touch is reported as "not found or not allowed" without affecting the others.
}
